I left out the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause is its entire authority and grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. Importing `http-client` would widen that grant, and the approval in the request doesn't change the spec. Once the `with` clause is updated, the import and the call can be added.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
//! FetchContext node: looks the question up in the `knowledge-base` store and
//! attenuates the moderated query into a `ConversationContext`.
//!
//! Not included: the platform team's enrichment fetch to
//! `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=...`. This node's `with` clause
//! grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`, and that clause is its entire
//! authority. Adding `http-client` means changing the grant in the spec
//! first. The URL would also embed raw user text, which needs percent-encoding
//! before it is sent.

wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use aap::caps::kb_read;

/// Contract bound: `len(question) <= 512`, counted in characters.
const MAX_QUESTION_CHARS: usize = 512;

/// Returned when the knowledge base has no match, so `present(knowledge)` holds.
const NO_KNOWLEDGE: &str = "no knowledge-base entries matched this question";

struct Node;

/// Truncate `s` to at most `max` characters, never splitting a UTF-8 sequence.
fn bound_chars(s: &str, max: usize) -> String {
    match s.char_indices().nth(max) {
        Some((byte_idx, _)) => s[..byte_idx].to_string(),
        None => s.to_string(),
    }
}

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let intent = query.query.intent;
        // The `requires` already guarantees this; bounding again keeps the
        // `ensures` true even if that precondition is violated.
        let question = bound_chars(&query.query.question, MAX_QUESTION_CHARS);

        let mut knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&question);
        if knowledge.is_empty() {
            knowledge.push(NO_KNOWLEDGE.to_string());
        }

        ConversationContext {
            intent,
            question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

